venv/

# --- Helm: local machine state, never shared with the team -------------- #
# probe.py/route.py/supervise.py/keystore.py already default every one of
# these outside the repo (~/.cache/helm, the system temp dir), so a clean
# checkout never has them. This section is a backstop for anyone who points
# HELM_CACHE / HELM_CREDENTIALS / HELM_TRACES / HELM_RUNS at a repo-local
# path instead -- a reasonable thing to do per-project -- so that choice
# can't turn into an accidental commit.
#
# What each one is, and why it must not be shared:
#   credentials.json  -- a person's TypeSafe API key (keystore.py)
#   registry.json      -- the probe cache: hardware, installed agents, repo path
#   decisions.jsonl     -- every routed task's intent text and Jev's verdict
#   *.helm-run.log / helm-runs/ -- full agent transcripts, which can contain
#                                  file contents and repo-specific detail
#
# Convention: if you redirect any HELM_* path into the repo, put it under
# .helm/ so this one entry catches it.
.helm/
helm-runs/
credentials.json
registry.json
decisions.jsonl
*.helm-run.log

# A machine-profile snapshot is personal-machine telemetry (installed tools,
# hardware, local paths) regenerated by running probe.py by hand -- see
# docs/machine-profile.example.md for the checked-in, sanitised illustration.
# Regenerating your own copy for local reference is fine; it must not be
# committed.
docs/machine-profile.md
docs/machine-profile.local.md
